[[2047,16,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The optional services relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J60 controls\nthe circuit for the rear electric windows, as well as the sun roof\nand heated seats:  \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 See\n\t\tE3060\n\t\tSUN ROOF\n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 , \n\n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 See\n\t\tE3075\n\t\tHEATED SEATS\n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 and \n\n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 See\n\t\tE3076\n\t\tELECTRICALLY-ADJUSTABLE SEATS\n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 .</strong></p><p>The coil for relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J60 is energized when\nthe ignition is switched on (INT/A) by the line for fuse F6 for\nadditional fuse box B98B, whilst the supply at the relay contact\narrives from the battery, from the line for maxifuse J/B2 (of B99).</strong></p><p>This supply, passes through the rear electric\nwindow fuses \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F2 and F3 of B98 B, which guarantees the protection\nof the circuit and arrives at the switches in the front driver&#x27;s\ndoor (H45 left and H46 right).</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               The supply of the switches is\ntherefore controlled by the ignition (INT/A) and they are connected\nto earth \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>C20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               (in this way they are also lit up when the ignition\nis switched on).</p><p>When these switches are operated, they send\ncommand signals (positive and negative) to the switches in the rear\ndoors and from there to the (left) \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N65</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and right \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N66</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               motors:\nreversing the signals according to the contact which is closed determines\nthe direction of rotation of the actual motor.</p><p>The same supply controlled by the ignition\n(INT/A) also reaches the switches in the rear doors \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H53</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H54</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ,\npassing through the safety switch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H55</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , but only if it is\nin the enablement position. If this is not the case, the supply\nto the rear door switches is stopped.</p><p>Similar to the front switches, when the\nrear switches are activated, they send command signals (positive\nand negative) to the (left) \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N65</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and (right) \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N66</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               motors:\nreversing the signals according to the contact which has been closed, determines\nthe direction of rotation of the actual motor.</p>"]]